# DDCS Studio — System Roadmap

*Generated from architecture session — June 2026*

-----

## Vision

A CNC control and authoring system for DDCS controllers that works **offline by default**, requires **no hosted infrastructure**, and gives every user optional remote access — either through their own network or their own cloud account. fairy.exe is its own server. No third party sits in the data path unless the user chooses one.

- **fairy.exe** — runs on the shop PC, owns the machine, serves its own HTTPS
- **Studio** — authors programs, submits jobs, tracks progress
- **Transport adapters** — optional, user-configured, provider-agnostic

-----

## Core Principles

- No cloud required — ever — for any feature
- No Frédéric-hosted infrastructure for other users
- fairy is a self-contained HTTPS server accessible on LAN or externally via user’s own network config
- Vanilla JS, no build step
- Transport is a pluggable interface — provider doesn’t matter to the app
- Cloud adapters are a fallback for users who can’t control their network, not the default

-----

## Responsibility Split

|Concern                       |fairy (gateway)|Studio               |
|------------------------------|---------------|---------------------|
|Talk to DDCS controller       |✅              |❌                    |
