## Phase 3 — fairy.exe (distributable HTTPS server)

**Goal:** single executable, zero install, serves its own HTTPS, reachable on LAN wirelessly and optionally from anywhere via user’s own network.

**HTTPS on LAN**

- [ ] Generate self-signed cert on first run via `mkcert` (installs fairy as local CA — browsers trust it automatically, requires one-time admin rights)
- [ ] fairy binds to `0.0.0.0:443` (or `8443`) — reachable from any device on the WiFi
- [ ] Advertise `cnc-fairy.local` via mDNS (Bonjour/Avahi) — stable hostname regardless of IP
- [ ] Any phone/tablet on same WiFi opens `https://cnc-fairy.local` — no app install needed

**External access (user’s own network — no cloud)**

- [ ] Setup guide built into fairy UI:
  - Detect public IP
  - Test if port is open (checks from inside)
  - Walk through DuckDNS hostname registration
  - Auto-configure Let’s Encrypt cert for the DuckDNS hostname
  - Auto-renewal in background
- [ ] `direct.js` transport uses the configured external hostname
- [ ] External access is opt-in — LAN-only is the default

**First-run wizard**

- [ ] Machine IP / hostname (DDCS controller address)
- [ ] Axis count
- [ ] Controller version → loads controller profile
- [ ] Transport selection: Local LAN only / + External (self-hosted) / + Cloud

**Packaging**

- [ ] Bundle with pywebview into `fairy.exe`
- [ ] `bundle_standalone.py` updated to follow `../../shared/` imports
- [ ] Windows installer handles mDNS dependency (Bonjour)

