## Phase 6 — Cloud transport adapters (fallback for restricted networks)

**Goal:** users who can’t do port forwarding (apartment, corporate network, shared WiFi) can still get remote access via their own cloud account. Frédéric hosts nothing.

Ship in order of user-friendliness:

- [ ] `transports/dropbox.js` — OAuth2, files in `/Apps/DDCS-Studio/queue/`
- [ ] `transports/gdrive.js` — OAuth2, files in Drive app folder
- [ ] `transports/onedrive.js` — OAuth2, files in OneDrive app folder
- [ ] `transports/supabase.js` — connection string, best realtime option
- [ ] `transports/s3.js` — S3-compatible (covers AWS, Backblaze B2, Wasabi)

Each adapter is independent — a broken `gdrive.js` never affects `lan.js`.
OAuth tokens stored locally in fairy, never leave the machine.
Community can contribute new adapters by implementing the 4-method interface.

